  "repository": "once-campfire-mojo",
  "changes": [
    "Owned byte buffers now carry socket data, HTTP bodies, uploads/downloads, compressed responses, WebSocket frames/fragments, Marshal values, keys, hashes and ciphertext. Text decoding validates UTF-8 explicitly.",
    "All Mojo FFI and raw-pointer APIs are confined to src/native_boundary.mojo. Typed wrappers check lengths, capacities, cryptographic key sizes, native descriptor ranges and C-string NULs; returned allocations are copied and freed inside that boundary.",
    "Native SQL resources are owned together and statements reset on failure. DOM addresses were replaced with opaque validated identifiers that invalidate freed nodes/attributes and tolerate repeated cleanup.",
    "The rest of the Mojo audit also fixed malformed signature byte slicing, invalid percent-encoded UTF-8 handling, single-character quoted fields, helper range/allocation checks, complete framing size limits, and minimum-integer Marshal encoding.",
    "Seven new HTTP/WebSocket cases verify malformed-input rejection without worker replacement. Native and independent binary regressions plus a source-boundary guard run in both CI architectures. A pre-existing cleanup-test observation race now waits for both file removal and durable SQL completion."
  ],
