  "method": "Native ARM64 Linux in Docker Desktop on the same Apple M4 (24 GiB). Three rotating rounds, 2-second warmups, 8-second samples, 16 keep-alive clients accepting gzip, 64 MiB response caches, server CPUs 0\u20133 and client CPUs 4\u20137. SQLite WAL synchronous=FULL, atomic outbox, persisted recipient receipts and a common 10-second SQLite write-lock budget. Posting rates include final job drain. No builds or other task tests ran during timing.",
  "limits": "Rust and C use the previously documented local durability patches. Timed posts exercise three identical push endpoint-policy rejections; external push encryption/network delivery and connected Cable subscribers are outside these five timed workloads and have separate correctness tests. External delivery remains at-least-once across a crash after provider acceptance. This compares implementations under one stated configuration, not intrinsic language speed.",
